@code{C-h v} on any option says more.  For code that extends readq@comma{} @code{C-h f
readq-define-viewer} explains how to support another document viewer@comma{}
and the hooks are listed by @samp{M-x apropos-variable RET ^readq-.*-\(hook\|functions\)}.

Two functions are there for other packages that want to add to the
queue.  @samp{(readq-current-book)} returns the book of the queue shown in
the current buffer@comma{} or nil.  @samp{(readq-add-extract TEXT :book BOOK :page
PAGE :title TITLE :tags TAGS)} adds TEXT as an extract of BOOK (the
book shown in the current buffer when BOOK is left out) and returns
it; with @samp{:keep t} it is kept as a note@comma{} out of the queue@comma{} as with
@code{C-c r E}.  my-gptel-study uses them for @code{C-c C-e} in an answer
buffer.  @code{C-h f} on either says more.

@node When something goes wrong
@chapter When something goes wrong

@findex readq-mode
@vindex readq-mode
@vindex readq-mpv-program
@vindex readq-daily-minutes
@findex readq-doctor

Start with @code{C-c r ?}.  It finds most problems and says what to do.

@itemize
@item
@strong{A book doesn't open at my place.}  Is @samp{readq-mode} on?  Did the file
move?  Then press @code{l} on it in the dashboard to point readq to the new
place.
@item
@strong{SumatraPDF doesn't save my page.}  readq learns it when you close
the document in SumatraPDF@.  Keep its option @emph{Remember opened files}
on.
@item
@strong{mpv doesn't start.}  Check that @samp{mpv} runs in a terminal@comma{} or set
@samp{readq-mpv-program}.  For YouTube@comma{} update yt-dlp.
@item
@strong{Anki export fails.}  Open Anki first@comma{} with AnkiConnect installed.
@item
@strong{A figure shows as a link.}  Press @code{C-c C-x C-v} in the note to show
images.
@item
@strong{readq says the queue file changed and was not saved.}  Another Emacs@comma{}
or a sync program@comma{} wrote it.  See @ref{Your data, , Your data}.
@item
@strong{Too much is due.}  Lower the priority of what matters less@comma{} pause
books you are not reading now (@code{x})@comma{} or lower @samp{readq-daily-minutes}:
readq spreads the rest.
@end itemize

The full list of changes is in @uref{https://github.com/n0w1ht/readq/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md, CHANGELOG.md}.  Problems and ideas go to
@uref{https://github.com/n0w1ht/readq/issues, the issue tracker}.

